INT. BACK ROOM OF A TAXIDERMY SHOP - NIGHT

Glass eyes. Stuffed owls. A badger mid-snarl. A card table with four chairs and one bare bulb.

ROCCO "THE BOOKKEEPER" VANTI, 50s, rolled sleeves, counts cash into neat stacks. SAL MAROUNI, 30s, tracksuit, bounces a knee. LENA FISHBACH, 40s, wire glasses, watches the door. TIMOTHY BLACKWOOD-ADE, 20s, nervous, holds a duffel bag in his lap.

ROCCO
Eighty. Eighty-five. Ninety.

SAL
Where's the rest?

ROCCO
Counting, Sal.

LENA
Timothy, put the bag on the table.

TIMOTHY
It's fine here.

SAL
Put it on the table.

TIMOTHY
I said it's fine.

LENA
Why are you sweating?

TIMOTHY
It's hot.

SAL
It's a taxidermy shop in November.

TIMOTHY
The badger gives off heat.

ROCCO
(not looking up)
Ninety-five. A hundred.

Lena shifts her chair. A floorboard creaks somewhere above them. Timothy flinches.

SAL
Who else is here?

TIMOTHY
Nobody.

LENA
There's a second floor?

ROCCO
Storage.

SAL
Check it.

LENA
I'll check it.

ROCCO
Sit down, Lena.

LENA
Rocco, there's something up there.

ROCCO
It's a possum. Frank keeps one on a branch.

SAL
Dead?

ROCCO
Obviously dead.

The ceiling creaks again. All four look up. The bulb sways. A shadow slides across the badger's snout.

TIMOTHY
That didn't sound dead.

LENA
That sounded like a person.

SAL
Give me the bag.

TIMOTHY
No.

SAL
Give me the bag, Timothy.

TIMOTHY
I can't.

ROCCO
(slowly setting down the money)
Why not?

TIMOTHY
Because it's not the money.

Silence. The bulb swings. Sal's hand drifts toward his jacket. Lena eases her chair back.

LENA
Then what is it?

TIMOTHY
I didn't have a choice. They said bring it or --

ROCCO
Who said?

TIMOTHY
The man upstairs.

The ceiling groans. Footsteps cross to the top of the stairs. A silhouette fills the doorway above. Boots descend one step at a time.

SAL
(whispering)
Rocco.

ROCCO
Everybody stay calm.

LENA
I'm calm.

SAL
I'm not calm.

TIMOTHY
He said don't run.

The boots reach the bottom stair. A hand reaches out and flicks off the bulb. Dark. Glass eyes gleam in the red glow of an exit sign.

ROCCO
(a hush)
Nobody move.
